  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41159804",
      "title": "Triggering Cache Revalidations",
      "lectureOrder": 128,
      "videoOrder": 119,
      "sourceHash": "eed37eccc751b7abd8f27f75b906817d35943070850273e731514184c261d659",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 3.12,
          "en": "So how can we fix this problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.12,
          "end": 6.993,
          "en": "of NextJS caching too aggressively?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.16,
          "end": 13.16,
          "en": "Well, we need to tell NextJS to throw away its cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.32,
          "end": 17.793,
          "en": "or parts of its cache whenever we add a new meal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 18.69,
          "end": 21.66,
          "en": "And of course, this is such a common requirement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 21.66,
          "end": 24.57,
          "en": "that there's a built-in method for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.57,
          "end": 28.47,
          "en": "a built-in function provided by NextJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 28.47,
          "end": 32.34,
          "en": "a function which I wanna execute in my server action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.34,
          "end": 36.273,
          "en": "right after saving a meal before I redirect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 37.23,
          "end": 41.703,
          "en": "And that function is called revalidatePath.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 43.74,
          "end": 46.71,
          "en": "This function tells NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 46.71,
          "end": 50.1,
          "en": "to revalidate the cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 50.1,
          "end": 53.403,
          "en": "that belongs to a certain route path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 54.66,
          "end": 57.24,
          "en": "So for example, if I know that I want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 57.24,
          "end": 58.83,
          "en": "to visit the meals page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 58.83,
          "end": 63.12,
          "en": "and that the meals page depends on data that changed now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 63.12,
          "end": 68.07300000000001,
          "en": "I can tell NextJS to revalidate the /meals path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 69.03,
          "end": 72.123,
          "en": "And with that, that path would be revalidated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 73.53,
          "end": 75.84,
          "en": "Now what's important is that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 75.84,
          "end": 79.8,
          "en": "by default, only that path will be revalidated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 79.8,
          "end": 81.543,
          "en": "no nested paths.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 82.47,
          "end": 86.73,
          "en": "So if I had some nested path there in my meals folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 86.73,
          "end": 89.61,
          "en": "that also depends on all the meals data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 89.61,
          "end": 92.583,
          "en": "I would have to revalidate that separately.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 93.66,
          "end": 96.69,
          "en": "Alternatively, you can pass a second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 96.69,
          "end": 100.563,
          "en": "to revalidate path and set this to layout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 101.46000000000001,
          "end": 105.03,
          "en": "The default is page, which means that simply this one page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 105.03,
          "end": 108.53999999999999,
          "en": "for this one path will be revalidated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 108.53999999999999,
          "end": 110.28,
          "en": "If you set it to layout,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 110.28,
          "end": 113.67,
          "en": "it's the layout that will be revalidated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 113.67,
          "end": 116.97,
          "en": "which as you learned, also wraps nested pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 116.97,
          "end": 118.59,
          "en": "and therefore, with this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 118.59,
          "end": 122.463,
          "en": "all nested pages would be revalidated as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 123.36,
          "end": 125.43,
          "en": "And revalidate simply means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 125.43,
          "end": 129.63,
          "en": "that NextJS throws away the cache that is associated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 129.63,
          "end": 131.49,
          "en": "with those pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 131.49,
          "end": 135.033,
          "en": "So, for example, the cached pages themselves.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 136.44,
          "end": 139.26,
          "en": "Now here, I don't care about any nested pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 139.26,
          "end": 143.19,
          "en": "because the dynamic page here isn't pre-generated anyways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 143.19,
          "end": 144.78,
          "en": "in our current setup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 144.78,
          "end": 148.23,
          "en": "and the share page doesn't depend on the meals data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 148.23,
          "end": 152.043,
          "en": "So I'm fine with just revalidating /meals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 152.94,
          "end": 155.46,
          "en": "If you would want to revalidate all the pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 155.46,
          "end": 158.49,
          "en": "of your entire website, you could, by the way, do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 158.49,
          "end": 161.793,
          "en": "by targeting slash and then setting the mode to layout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 163.07999999999998,
          "end": 166.773,
          "en": "But here, I'm fine with just revalidating the meals path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 168.48,
          "end": 173.48,
          "en": "Well, and with that done, if we now run npm run build again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 174.09,
          "end": 176.49,
          "en": "to build all those pages again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 176.49,
          "end": 179.94,
          "en": "they will still be pre-generated and cached,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 179.94,
          "end": 183.21,
          "en": "but now that cache should be revalidated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 183.21,
          "end": 187.053,
          "en": "and partially cleared once we added a new meal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 188.22,
          "end": 190.47,
          "en": "So if I now run npm start again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 190.47,
          "end": 193.05,
          "en": "to start that development server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 193.05,
          "end": 195.423,
          "en": "and I then add another new meal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 200.34,
          "end": 203.673,
          "en": "like this, picking the same image as always,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 205.05,
          "end": 206.463,
          "en": "if I submit that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 208.62,
          "end": 211.86,
          "en": "it takes a bit longer here, which is a good sign",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 211.86,
          "end": 213.27,
          "en": "because it's taking longer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 213.27,
          "end": 216.32999999999998,
          "en": "because it loaded all those meals again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 216.32999999999998,
          "end": 220.29,
          "en": "And here we are, now the image is missing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 220.29,
          "end": 222.32999999999998,
          "en": "we'll take care of that in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 222.32999999999998,
          "end": 227.32999999999998,
          "en": "But the meal is there and that's of course a good sign.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 227.64,
          "end": 231.87,
          "en": "In addition, we got these Fetching meals logs back here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 231.87,
          "end": 235.263,
          "en": "which also proves that this is now working as intended.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
